INT. REGIONAL AIRPORT - GATE B - NIGHT

Empty chairs, a dim terminal. A departure board flickers: ALL FLIGHTS DELAYED. Rain streaks the windows onto a runway of dark glass.

FINN LARKSPUR-MBEKI, 30s, rumpled, sits with a coffee and a boarding pass, scribbling in a notebook.

Across the aisle, WILHELMINA "MINA" OSTROWSKI, 30s, clutches a small suitcase and stares at the floor, thumb worrying a loose ring on her finger.

Two seats down, an old couple, GRANDPA TOBIAS and GRANDMA ESME ADEBAYO, 70s, share a thermos, bickering softly.

                    TANNOY (V.O.)
Attention passengers. Flight 418 to Denver is delayed until further notice.

A collective groan. Finn caps his pen.

                    FINN
(to the room)
Of course it is.

Mina looks up. Their eyes meet. She glances away first.

                    FINN (CONT'D)
(to Mina)
Long night.

                    MINA
Seems so.

                    FINN
You headed to Denver?

                    MINA
Eventually.

                    FINN
Me too. Business. You?

                    MINA
A wedding.

                    FINN
Whose?

                    MINA
Mine.

Finn blinks. Nods slowly. Looks at the ring on her finger.

                    FINN
Congratulations?

                    MINA
Ask me in Denver.

He smiles. She almost does too. The old couple, across the aisle, are unabashedly listening.

                    ESME
(to Tobias)
I told you she was nervous.

                    TOBIAS
She's not nervous, she's sulking.

                    ESME
Nervous.

                    TOBIAS
^
Sulking.

They glare at each other. Mina and Finn share a quiet look, and for the first time, both of them laugh.

                    FINN
What's his name?

                    MINA
Gordon.

                    FINN
Gordon.

                    MINA
He's very kind.

                    FINN
That's a good thing.

                    MINA
It is.

                    FINN
But?

                    MINA
But nothing. He's kind.

She stands. Walks to the window, her reflection lost against the rain. Finn watches her back. He tears a page from his notebook, folds it, hesitates, then puts it in his pocket.

                    TANNOY (V.O.)
Attention. Flight 418 will board in fifteen minutes.

Silence. Everyone looks up at the speaker.

                    MINA
(to the window)
Fifteen minutes.

                    FINN
Enough time for a coffee.

                    MINA
Enough time for anything.

She turns. Their eyes meet again. She crosses back and sits beside him, not across from him.

                    MINA (CONT'D)
Tell me something true.

                    FINN
I don't like Denver.

                    MINA
That's not it.

                    FINN
I'm going because I'm afraid to stay.

                    MINA
Of what?

                    FINN
Of the place I'm supposed to be.

She breathes out. Her hand finds his on the armrest. For a moment neither moves.

                    TANNOY (V.O.)
Final boarding call for Flight 418.

The old couple stand, collecting thermos and coats. Esme pauses at the end of the aisle, looks down at the pair of them.

                    ESME
Go on, dears. Or don't. But decide.

                    TOBIAS
Esme.

                    ESME
^
What? I'm eighty. I get to say.

She takes his arm and leads him toward the jetway. Finn and Mina watch them go. Then Mina slides the ring off her finger, slowly, and holds it in her open palm between them.

                    MINA
(to herself)
Well. Here we are.

Finn closes her fingers around the ring. The board above them flickers once more and goes dark.
